 "short_name": "Lesedi",
 "_doc": "Lesedi LM (Heidelberg). Two renders of one statement: (A) cabedocs print (8 bills) and (B) eMunsoft print (2 bills, 2026). Both: header 'Account Number:' / 'Account Date: dd MON yyyy', a Meter Readings table (meter, type ELECTRICITY / KVA / WATER, old, new, [A/E flag in B], consumption, levied amount, reading dates) and an Account Details ledger with three money columns (ex VAT / VAT / incl). Render A prints readings with free decimals and drops empty cells (kVA rows lack the old reading; some rows have no consumption), so rows are matched in full and short shapes and their levied amounts summed separately. Several kWh meters per account: kWh summed, meters joined, readings only when one kWh meter exists, reading dates = first kWh row. Ledger 'ELECTRICITY' lines mix energy and demand, so standard_r / demand_r come from the meter-table levied amounts and other_r is BASIC ELECTRICITY; total_ex_vat_r = ledger ELECTRICITY + BASIC ELECTRICITY (ex column). Water, sewerage, refuse and rates rows from their ledger lines. Fingerprint: own VAT number + name. IDENTITY les_meter_identity_r = levied kWh + levied kVA (meter table) + basic: 0.00 on 10/10, 0 checks.",
